# Exclude everything except the API server and its single dependency.
# Without this, Docker copies 4GB+ (data/, mobile_app/node_modules, .git)
# which causes Railway builds to time out or take 10+ minutes.

# data/ is excluded child-by-child (the `data/*` glob form, not a single bare
# `data/` rule) so the negations below can re-include specific small files —
# Docker can't un-exclude a path whose parent was excluded via a bare `data/`
# rule. Found 2026-07-09: ops_runbook.md/ceo_learnings.md and every other
# knowledge_base reference doc never existed inside the container at all (on
# top of being ephemeral before a Volume existed) — this exclusion swallowed
# them outright. knowledge_base/ is ~700KB, negligible next to the ~4GB it's
# carved out of (digital_products/, backups/, and the many per-product dirs).
#
# Found 2026-07-09 (same day, second incident): the listing quality-gate JSON
# configs below were ALSO swallowed by this same blanket rule -- confirmed the
# hard way when tools/listing_compliance_sweep.py, triggered for the first
# time as a server-side workflow, returned FAIL for all 140/140 live listings
# (manifest.get(listing_id) was always None -> every listing looked
# "unmapped" -> fail-closed fired for the whole shop). The bad run's 140
# staged deactivate_listing actions were rejected and its 140 bogus todos
# deleted before Scott ever saw them, and nothing was actually deactivated
# (that needs a second, separate approval this code never got to). Same root
# cause almost certainly explains why `_quality_audit_loop` (main.py) and
# `_calendar_tasks_loop`'s seasonal-keyword checks, both of which read these
# same files, may have been running against empty config since whenever this
# `data/*` rule was first introduced -- not just introduced this session.
# All five files together are <135KB, negligible.
data/*
!data/knowledge_base
!data/registered_commands.json
!data/listing_manifest.json
!data/listing_rules.json
!data/listing_approvals.json
!data/product_art_registry.json
!data/dp_listing_map.json
!data/product_catalog.json
mobile_app/
.git/

# Python cruft
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
*.egg-info/

# Secrets (Railway injects these via env vars — never bake them in the image)
.env
*.env

# Dev / CI noise
.github/
.pytest_cache/
*.md
!data/knowledge_base/*.md

# Found 2026-09-05, and it is the THIRD time this file's blanket rules have
# swallowed a doc the server actively tries to read at runtime (see the two
# 2026-07-09 incidents documented above).
#
# `*.md` matches root-level markdown only -- a single `*` does not cross `/`,
# which is why `**/*.go`-style patterns exist -- so CLAUDE.md has been excluded
# from every image ever built here. main.py's `_resolve_kb_doc` special-cases
# "CLAUDE.md" and Frank's own system prompt tells it to read that file for the
# full 3D printer specs, quality-gate rules, product catalog and autonomy
# boundaries. In the container that call can only ever have 404'd.
#
# The `.claude/skills/**` line is belt-and-braces: by the same root-only rule
# those nested SKILL.md files should already survive `*.md`, but this file's
# own history says do not bet a runtime read path on a subtle glob semantic.
# Both are a few hundred KB against the ~4GB this file exists to carve down.
!CLAUDE.md
!.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md

# Local DB (never ship into the image)
**/hub_data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
